    "bodySha256": "e6c4a6bf295d28bb6721b13bed89f700c32daa046a70c2305dc2454ca170159a",
    "body": "# omp-spec-kit v1.1.0\n\n## Included changes\n\n- Promotes the bounded 10-tool MCP surface to the stable major release: 9 read-only tools and one transactional `spec_patch` authoring tool.\n- Preserves bounded entity, graph, document, evidence, and Markdown queries with pagination, projections, cursors, and traversal limits.\n- Verifies the complete semantic tool-E2E matrix against the built server and the exact release archive launcher.\n\n## Verified release\n\n- Candidate digest: `c2dcbb9dbdd358f0cf41add3c666a8a7eb5f0ceadbaf9c49e589b0609a370c5d`\n- Package tree digest: `5dd69d7204abede7008434a907d7ffda75101afedaba1e8cd488bf28fd32d2ef`\n- Archive SHA-256: `7cfc72e6b5679849fef279bb8988d549f6a2b25642c608a9389d61c1b370d520`\n- Peeled tag commit: `bcf4868079cb508a78b71c92e1e326a6e6ff98a1`\n- OMP runtime: `18.0.11`\n- Distribution evidence: lifecycle producers, Docker BDD, manager discovery, and nine closed MRI receipts.\n\nInstall or upgrade at project scope, reload plugin metadata, then start a fresh OMP session before invoking MCP tools.\n"
